<!--
  Merge these into android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml after
  `npx cap add android`. Capacitor scaffolds a manifest with INTERNET only,
  which is not enough for this app:

    - ACCESS_COARSE_LOCATION / ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION
      The position layer calls navigator.geolocation from the webview.
      Capacitor's BridgeWebChromeClient.onGeolocationPermissionsShowPrompt
      does request these at runtime, but Android refuses an undeclared
      permission outright, without showing a dialog, so the layer reports
      "denied" and there is nothing on screen to explain why.

    - uses-feature ... required="false"
      Declaring a location permission implies the hardware feature, which
      would hide the app on Play from devices without GPS. The map is fully
      usable without a fix, so opt back out.

    - android:allowBackup="false" on <application>
      The app stores nothing worth restoring (no accounts, no settings that
      survive a reinstall) and Play's Data safety form is easier to answer
      honestly without auto-backup in the picture.

  `density` is already in the MainActivity configChanges list as of
  Capacitor 8; without it the webview reloads when the app is resized.
-->

<uses-permission android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_COARSE_LOCATION" />
<uses-permission android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION" />

<uses-feature android:name="android.hardware.location.gps" android:required="false" />
<uses-feature android:name="android.hardware.location" android:required="false" />
